00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:38,237
It's time to laugh at the end
of the day I'll be laughing at

2
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:40,677
the end of the day I'll be laughing

3
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:46,877
at the end of the day I'll be

4
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:52,717
laughing at the end of the day
Crazy Crazy Rainbow Star Drink

5
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:48,160
You've now arrived at 47th cruise station.

6
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:52,744
Please check all of your belongings
before departing the C train.

7
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:02,278
If you want to take it, I'll
give it to you for free.

8
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:04,540
Since you're a real swordsman.

9
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:10,050
Damn it.

10
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:15,196
This year's Aqua Laguna did
a real number on the city.

11
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:21,257
Everyone's giving it their best, but I
don't think we can repair this on our own.

12
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:22,580
What is that?

13
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,700
It's Polly from Doc 1!

14
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:29,492
What's he doing here on the back streets?

15
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:33,020
Quiet down!

16
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:35,820
We're here to work, Doc Clay. Now move!

17
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:41,597
Doc 3, I'm leaving this
side of the bridge to you.

18
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:42,510
Yes, sir!

19
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:46,037
Doc 5, you get started with the
houses next to Scrap Island.

20
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:46,950
Yes, sir!

21
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:49,520
I know we still gotta do our day jobs,

22
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:52,817
but I want to see this whole town in
tip-top shape by the end of the month!

23
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:53,730
Yeah!

24
00:02:53,813 --> 00:02:54,643
Yeah!

25
00:02:54,726 --> 00:02:55,556
Let's go! Yeah!

26
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:58,390
Thanks, guys.

27
00:02:58,480 --> 00:02:59,833
We love you, Kelly Law.

28
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,960
They never let us down.

29
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:14,260
Ah, jeez.

30
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:16,257
Building stuff sure is hard work.

31
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:18,897
I admit, we're a lot
better at breaking things.

32
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:20,477
Guess we're sleeping outdoors again.

33
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:21,460
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

34
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:24,640
There you go. Good.

35
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:26,200
You take it easy.

36
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:28,977
Just a little rest and
you'll be better in no time.

37
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:35,377
Reindeer said Gamora's eyesight should
return if he takes it easy for a while.

38
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:37,100
Oh, really? That's great.

39
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:42,920
Come on, let us meet the pirates.

40
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:45,817
We want to apologize for
treating them so bad before.

41
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:46,730
No way.

42
00:03:46,813 --> 00:03:48,497
The Straw Hats aren't
meeting with anyone today.

43
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:50,577
Our company prepared
them a thank you package.

44
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:52,117
At least let us give it to them.

45
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,553
I'm with Warner 7 News.

46
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:56,277
Can I please get a comment with
the heroes who saved the mayor?

47
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:57,190
No means no.

48
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,277
They're busy, okay?

49
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:59,437
Please let me take a picture.

50
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:00,577
All of you, go home!

51
00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:02,778
Is the secretary to replace Kaliput?

52
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:16,450
Awesome.

53
00:04:16,533 --> 00:04:17,897
Now that's what I call power.

54
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:19,257
Is this where you wanted it?

55
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:20,857
Yeah, that's perfect, thanks.

56
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:22,777
Wish we had you guys around all the time.

57
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:24,997
This kind of stuff is a piece of cake.

58
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:27,080
If you got more, then bring it on.

59
00:04:29,420 --> 00:04:31,949
You're making everyone
else look bad, guys.

60
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:34,660
By the way, Sniper King,

61
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:38,340
you, sure you're happy here? Huh?

62
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:40,945
Because we were just thinking.

63
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:44,437
If our bosses are still fighting
like you said they were,

64
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:47,717
there's no point in us joining up
with them until it's all settled.

65
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:50,517
We'll stick around here and
help out while they need it.

66
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:53,097
But after that, we plan
to head back to Elbath.

67
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:56,062
Long story short, you want
to come along with us?

68
00:04:59,020 --> 00:04:59,850
I don't know.

69
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,230
I see.

70
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:10,132
So in the end, you burned the blueprints.

71
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:12,306
I think it's better that way.

72
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:17,644
You've made yourself an
enemy of the government.

73
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:25,577
Yeah i guess so spill it what are
you so busy drawing over there bro

74
00:05:25,660 --> 00:05:30,397
Aqua Laguna was powerful This year
i'm sure it's weighing on everyone's

75
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:34,037
minds it may not be long before
this island is completely swallowed

76
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:41,000
by the sea so what's the plan
i'm going to make this city float

77
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:42,390
What?

78
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:45,437
You're gonna make Water 7 a boat?

79
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,932
Do you really think that's even possible?

80
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,637
Have you forgotten already?

81
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:54,544
We grew up watching a man who
could make the impossible possible.

82
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:57,457
Now I'm going to do the same.

83
00:05:57,540 --> 00:06:00,920
If you're a man, show some gusto.

84
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:05,700
He did always do everything
with a bang, didn't he?

85
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:11,370
Hello?

86
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:13,140
Oh, is that you, bro?

87
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:15,360
Hey, it's Amba. What's up?

88
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:16,777
You're gonna love this.

89
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:18,000
It finally came in.

90
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:20,897
We're picking it up here at
the train station as we speak.

91
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:23,100
Your 200 million buried treasure.

92
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:25,700
Ah, this is gonna be sweet.

93
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,960
Hope everyone's decent. Oh, hey, Kokoro.

94
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,557
Yo, we're coming through.

95
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,917
Sure, good to see you.

96
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,020
Yeah, yeah!

97
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:47,610
Get him!

98
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:55,580
I think you'd better wait outside.

99
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:03,737
You boys have been sleeping for days.

100
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:05,897
You must have been awfully pooped.

101
00:07:05,980 --> 00:07:08,780
Not that I blame you
after all that fighting.

102
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:10,380
Well, Mr.

103
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:12,696
Pirate King is back on his feet, too.

104
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:15,080
Uh, actually, not so much.

105
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:16,797
And what's that supposed to mean?

106
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:19,117
Even though he couldn't
move after the last fight,

107
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:22,376
he didn't want to miss dinner
because he was sleeping.

108
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:27,020
So he developed the sleep-eating
technique you see here.

109
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,280
He's still asleep?

110
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:31,160
Whoa, that's so cool! Yeah!

111
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:34,580
That's what you call multi-talented.

112
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:41,135
By the way, your Log Pose should be
set after another two or three days.

113
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:43,500
What is what happened?

114
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:50,680
Even if the Log Pose is set, it's not
like we can go anywhere without a ship.

115
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:56,000
All the money we saved up to
buy a new ship is gone forever.

116
00:07:56,320 --> 00:08:01,160
Our clothes, furniture, Even Bellamere's
precious tangerine trees were lost.

117
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:03,362
Aqua Laguna carried it all away.

118
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:05,738
I'm so depressed, I can't even move.

119
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:08,801
We left our stuff in one
of the Backstreet Hotels.

120
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:12,840
Oh, so that's what your
guests are here about.

121
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,190
Our guests?

122
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:15,640
My trees!

123
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:19,000
Oh my gosh, I thought
I'd never see them again!

124
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:20,697
I'm so happy!

125
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:24,657
Yeah, sorry about kicking you out, but we
thought you tried to assassinate Iceberg.

126
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:28,357
We treated your belongings as pirate
loot, so we confiscated everything.

127
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:29,477
I hope you're not mad.

128
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:30,837
Of course I'm not mad!

129
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:31,979
Thank you so much!

130
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:33,858
Well, there you go!

131
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:35,450
Hi!

132
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:36,810
Dr.

133
00:08:36,893 --> 00:08:37,723
Chopper reporting it!

134
00:08:37,806 --> 00:08:38,636
How are you?

135
00:08:38,719 --> 00:08:40,600
I'm great now that you're here!

136
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:42,660
Such a heavy back.

137
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:43,920
Please, allow me.

138
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:45,320
If you must.

139
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,537
I treated the Franky family's wounds,

140
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:50,597
but I didn't let Robin out of
my sight for a single second.

141
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:51,780
Mission complete.

142
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:55,737
I already told you,
I'm not going anywhere.

143
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:56,650
You promise?

144
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:59,140
You have my word, soldier. Guys, look!

145
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:00,257
Can you believe it?

146
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:02,120
My tangerine trees are okay!

147
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,417
We got our money back and our stuff, too!

148
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,330
Really?

149
00:09:05,413 --> 00:09:07,077
Once we buy a ship, then
we'll be good to go!

150
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:07,990
Oh, right!

151
00:09:08,073 --> 00:09:08,903
That's great!

152
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:17,360
Wow, baby!

153
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:20,160
You guys feeling super? Oh, what?

154
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:22,400
Oh, some folks aren't here.

155
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:23,910
Whatever.

156
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,417
What's with the big entrance?

157
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:26,618
Something going on?

158
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:28,050
You bet.

159
00:09:28,133 --> 00:09:30,420
Now, better listen close, brother.

160
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:37,400
So, there's this island
that's always at war.

161
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:40,577
If you're here to tell bedtime
stories, go bother someone else.

162
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:41,490
Shut up.

163
00:09:41,573 --> 00:09:42,403
This is important.

164
00:09:42,486 --> 00:09:43,316
Listen.

165
00:09:43,399 --> 00:09:45,380
For years, fire has rained on that island.

166
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:49,257
Death and destruction are the
only things that its people know.

167
00:09:49,340 --> 00:09:50,480
Houses burn down.

168
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:51,896
Cities fall to ruin.

169
00:09:52,020 --> 00:09:53,937
There's no place to
run from all the chaos.

170
00:09:54,020 --> 00:09:59,237
And in the midst of all this madness
there's a single tree no matter what

171
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:03,857
Happens it never falls and no matter how
much the island is destroyed its people

172
00:10:03,940 --> 00:10:09,097
Gather around it and build it all up
again it's the strongest tree in the

173
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:12,797
World as far as anyone knows only a few

174
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:17,197
exist it's known as the jewel tree Adam?

175
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:18,160
Huh?

176
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,840
Okay, so what?

177
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:26,012
Every so often a piece of wood from
that tree shows up on the black market.

178
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:31,540
I've wanted one for a long time now, but
the going price is 200 million berries.

179
00:10:31,980 --> 00:10:33,340
Too expensive for me.

180
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:34,690
That is,

181
00:10:34,773 --> 00:10:36,817
until a bunch of pirates
showed up flailing

182
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:39,097
their money around and
begging me to take it.

183
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:40,010
Bastard!

184
00:10:40,093 --> 00:10:42,917
You used our money to buy some stupid
log and then you brag about it?

185
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,420
Told you! Shut up!

186
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:55,620
A long time ago, I decided that I was done
building ships for the rest of my life.

187
00:10:56,220 --> 00:11:00,338
And yet, I couldn't help but follow
in the footsteps of my old master.

188
00:11:00,620 --> 00:11:03,502
And soon enough, I found
myself designing a ship.

189
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:10,740
Now, my hope is to use that
special wood to build it.

190
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:13,360
To put all my heart into one last ship.

191
00:11:13,620 --> 00:11:16,560
A ship of dreams that
can sail across any sea.

192
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:27,700
I've had the blueprints for ages.

193
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:30,080
Now I finally have the wood.

194
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:32,360
All that's left is to make it.

195
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:35,820
So, what I'm saying here?

196
00:11:37,020 --> 00:11:38,897
Is it would be my honor?

197
00:11:38,980 --> 00:11:40,397
If you'd take my ship?

198
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:42,940
and sail the world.

199
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:48,657
Wait, so does that mean...

200
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:51,660
You're gonna give us
the ship free of charge?

201
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:55,984
Uh-huh, cause that way I'll know
my masterpiece is in good hands.

202
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:58,356
Trust me, that's all I could ask for.

203
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:01,366
Well, that, and you kinda
paid for it already.

204
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:05,657
Gold Roger is the only man in history
who's sailed across the whole world,

205
00:12:05,740 --> 00:12:09,797
and his ship, the Otto Jackson, was
made from a jeweled tree as well.

206
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:11,080
Mark my words.

207
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:14,820
I'll show you the best
damn ship you've ever seen!

208
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:18,120
You're a shipwright after all.

209
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:23,185
You can pretend all you like, but in the
end, you're just like old Tom, ain't ya?

210
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:26,840
Guess you're right.

211
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:28,300
I get it now.

212
00:12:31,540 --> 00:12:32,820
It took a while.

213
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:37,784
But I think I finally understand
the pride Tom felt when he died.

214
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:39,570
Yeah!

215
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:44,260
You're the best, Franky! Thank you!

216
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:46,097
We'd be happy to take your ship!

217
00:12:46,180 --> 00:12:47,010
All right!

218
00:12:47,093 --> 00:12:49,840
Now, on to the next island!
Boopies! You're back!

219
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,057
We have a new ship!

220
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:52,300
Get him! Get him!

221
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:54,820
Get him! Get him!

222
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:06,797
This is bad!

223
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:09,577
I didn't think those bastards
would come after us so soon.

224
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:11,737
Damn it, I bet Luffy's
still sleeping, too.

225
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:14,055
I gotta warn him before it's too late.

226
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,270
No way.

227
00:13:20,780 --> 00:13:21,660
The ocean.

228
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:26,280
It's the Navy.

229
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:28,257
They're here to arrest the pirates.

230
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:31,857
Even after they save the mayor's
life, they won't show them any mercy.

231
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:33,800
Hey, you see that over there?

232
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:36,277
That's Vice Admiral Garp's ship.

233
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:37,937
Straight from headquarters.

234
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:39,500
Wait, did you say Garp?

235
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:43,580
The same Garp that nearly captured
Gold Roger over and over again?

236
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:45,520
He's a living legend.

237
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:48,617
They're not messing
around if they send him.

238
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:51,406
If they don't run, those
pirates are finished.

239
00:13:55,580 --> 00:13:58,120
I don't have time for this crap right now.

240
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:02,640
Well, would you look at that?

241
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:03,960
I guess he's lost.

242
00:14:04,900 --> 00:14:05,730
Huh.

243
00:14:05,813 --> 00:14:06,660
Well, that's too bad.

244
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,660
Hey, pal, are you lost?

245
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:11,780
You new around town? Turn around.

246
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:13,116
Let's see your face.

247
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:25,120
Now, hold on, sir.

248
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:27,297
The only person here is our president, Mr.

249
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:28,210
Iceberg.

250
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:29,550
Do it.

251
00:14:29,633 --> 00:14:31,117
I know you're hiding those pirates.

252
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:32,277
I swear, we're not.

253
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:33,637
Hey, you can't go inside.

254
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:34,550
Hold on!

255
00:14:34,633 --> 00:14:35,817
The Straw Hats are heroes!

256
00:14:35,900 --> 00:14:36,730
They shut up!

257
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:51,200
Alright, you two. Wait here. Yes, sir!

258
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:05,740
What the hell?

259
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:06,980
What's going on?

260
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:11,480
Pardon me, but are you
folks the Straw Hat Pirates?

261
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:16,517
You see, I have some friends here that
would like to share our word with Monkey D.

262
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:17,430
Luffy.

263
00:15:17,513 --> 00:15:18,343
The Navy.

264
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:22,580
Dumb kid.

265
00:15:22,940 --> 00:15:24,020
Never learns.

266
00:15:24,180 --> 00:15:25,651
Just as careless as ever.

267
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,030
What?

268
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:32,477
Damn, he's fast.

269
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:33,900
Rise and shine!

270
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:40,330
No!

271
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:45,000
No! That hurt! No! What happened?

272
00:15:45,220 --> 00:15:47,257
Why would one little
punch hurt you so much?

273
00:15:47,340 --> 00:15:48,537
You're made of robber!

274
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:52,460
It's because there is no
defense against a fist of love.

275
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:56,037
You've been getting in a lot
of trouble lately, haven't you?

276
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:56,950
Luffy.

277
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,430
Grandpa!

278
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:06,030
Wado?

279
00:16:10,180 --> 00:16:11,360
It's been a while.

280
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:16,800
I think you owe me an apology, boy.

281
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:19,460
You've been up to no good. Garp?

282
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:24,097
But isn't that the name of the Navy
hero that fought against Gold Roger?

283
00:16:24,180 --> 00:16:27,700
Luffy, is this Navy guy
really your grandpa? Sure is!

284
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:29,777
No matter what, don't try to fight him!

285
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:34,448
He'll kill you, just like he almost
killed me over and over when I was little.

286
00:16:38,540 --> 00:16:39,370
Now, now.

287
00:16:39,453 --> 00:16:41,535
You're gonna give them the wrong idea.

288
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:46,767
Although I admit, I did throw
you into a ravine that one time.

289
00:16:48,820 --> 00:16:51,526
And I left you in the
jungle a few times, too.

290
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:57,958
And sure, there were those times I
sent you sailing on those balloons.

291
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:02,677
But I didn't do it to kill
you I did it to make you a man

292
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:06,577
I see so this is where all of
Luffy's endurance comes from

293
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:10,297
this is why everything rolls
off when I left you an Ace with

294
00:17:10,380 --> 00:17:12,877
my friend for training I thought
everything would work out

295
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:17,837
fine but I turned my back and

296
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:19,937
you end up like this I wanted

297
00:17:20,020 --> 00:17:22,537
to make you into a navy man
you stinking ingrate how the

298
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:25,317
heck did you become a criminal
I told you a million times I

299
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:28,217
wanted to be a pirate it's not
my fault you wouldn't listen

300
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:30,957
This is all that damn Red
Hat's fault, the fool.

301
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:31,870
I...

302
00:17:31,953 --> 00:17:34,900
I wouldn't even be alive if
it wasn't for Saints! Shut up!

303
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:37,900
Shut up, huh?

304
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,957
Is that any way to speak to your grandpa?

305
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:41,680
Oh, right! I'm sorry!

306
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:42,957
What are all dead for?

307
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:45,097
A captain's been captured by the Marines!

308
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:46,010
Luffy!

309
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:49,220
Help! No! This is bad.

310
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:50,577
If we try to help Luffy,

311
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:54,366
then all those Marines outside
are gonna rush in and attack us.

312
00:17:56,460 --> 00:17:57,460
They're asleep?

313
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:02,100
Uh, so wait, what are
we supposed to do here?

314
00:18:02,340 --> 00:18:05,164
I've never been in a
situation like this before.

315
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:08,384
Oh no, did I fall asleep again?

316
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:16,772
Wake up and take your lecture like a man!

317
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:20,556
Don't you dare doze off on
me when I'm yelling at you!

318
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:27,769
If you don't show your grandpa some
respect, I'll have to beat it out of you.

319
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:31,960
I think I'm going to stay out of this one.

320
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:35,270
Giri?

321
00:18:35,353 --> 00:18:36,560
Are you kidding me?

322
00:18:37,420 --> 00:18:38,773
That's his grandfather?

323
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:42,057
Well, it's no wonder Luffy
never talked about his family.

324
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:43,260
This is crazy.

325
00:18:43,820 --> 00:18:44,650
Giri.

326
00:18:48,820 --> 00:18:51,317
Speaking of that red-headed
pirate friend of yours,

327
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:54,857
Do you have any clue what kind of
dangerous business he's involved in?

328
00:18:54,940 --> 00:18:58,293
No, I haven't heard anything
about Shanks in a long time.

329
00:18:58,580 --> 00:18:59,410
Is he okay?

330
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:00,441
What's he up to?

331
00:19:00,600 --> 00:19:02,240
Is he okay? Of course.

332
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:06,617
There's as many pirates out there
as there are stars in the sky.

333
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:08,857
But that redhead's one of the brightest.

334
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:11,469
He's in the same class
as Whitebeard, even.

335
00:19:11,580 --> 00:19:14,277
There are only four pirates
as powerful as that,

336
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:18,184
and they rule over the second half
of the Grand Line, like kings.

337
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,920
They're the four emperors.

338
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:24,777
The seven warlords and us folks of
the Navy have allied against them.

339
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:27,560
The idea is to create a balance of power.

340
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:31,557
If any one of these three forces
grew stronger than the others,

341
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:35,758
then the peace we worked so hard to
protect would come crumbling down.

342
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:41,080
I don't really get it,
but I'm glad he's okay.

343
00:19:42,060 --> 00:19:44,000
Man, brings back memories, huh?

344
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:49,157
Luffy has connections
to red-haired shanks?

345
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:51,534
That's where he got his Straw Hat from.

346
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:53,838
Shanks asked him to take care of it.

347
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:57,320
I had no idea he was such
an important guy, though.

348
00:19:57,860 --> 00:19:59,154
It's over here, Zoro!

349
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:01,912
Damn it, we're too late!

350
00:20:02,380 --> 00:20:04,262
Anyway, good luck with the Navy!

351
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:06,860
I'm sorry again!

352
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:09,077
We shouldn't have tried to mug you!

353
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:10,278
That was a mistake!

354
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:11,437
Don't worry about it.

355
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:13,137
Thanks for showing me the way here.

356
00:20:13,220 --> 00:20:14,050
See ya!

357
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:19,189
What's going on out there?

358
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:22,820
It's the pirate hunter.

359
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:25,727
He seems to be going on
some sort of rampage.

360
00:20:26,060 --> 00:20:27,942
Ah, he's from Luffy's crew, huh?

361
00:20:28,320 --> 00:20:29,700
He looks pretty tough.

362
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:33,520
Go ahead, you two. Give him hell. Sir!

363
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:44,760
Kukali knives, huh?

364
00:20:45,020 --> 00:20:47,844
Interesting choice of a
weapon you've got there.

365
00:20:49,340 --> 00:20:50,200
Zoro, stop!

366
00:20:50,440 --> 00:20:52,322
It's OK, we don't need to fight!

367
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:55,760
Hey, what was that for, you jerk?! Shame.

368
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:58,200
That technique!

369
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:13,620
Are you OK? What happened?

370
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:18,440
Boys, you're no match at all.

371
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:21,157
You're as tough as I thought you'd be.

372
00:21:21,240 --> 00:21:22,500
That was a nice one.

373
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:25,380
Anyway, I give.

374
00:21:29,060 --> 00:21:30,640
Hi, Luffy. Hi, Zoro.

375
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:32,999
It's been a while.

376
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,435
Do you know who I am?

377
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:36,930
No.

378
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:39,160
Look, it's me. It's Kobe.

379
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:41,724
You mean you don't remember me?

380
00:21:42,020 --> 00:21:42,850
Kobe, huh?

381
00:21:42,933 --> 00:21:43,763
Huh?

382
00:21:43,846 --> 00:21:44,676
Huh?

383
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:48,770
Kobe, huh?

384
00:21:50,040 --> 00:21:52,158
Well, I do have a friend named Kobe.

385
00:21:52,340 --> 00:21:55,217
But the Kobe I know is a
whole lot smaller than you.

386
00:21:55,300 --> 00:21:56,130
Sorry.

387
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:57,230
Nope.

388
00:21:57,313 --> 00:21:58,217
That's the right Kobe.

389
00:21:58,300 --> 00:22:01,065
The crybaby, good-for-nothing
Kobe from before.

390
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:03,080
No way!

391
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:05,460
Yeah, that's him.

392
00:22:05,780 --> 00:22:07,657
But why is he on the Grand Line?

393
00:22:07,740 --> 00:22:10,377
To be honest, I'm not a
commissioned Navy officer yet.

394
00:22:10,460 --> 00:22:12,737
But when I heard you
guys were in the area,

395
00:22:12,820 --> 00:22:16,349
I had to stop by and say hello
while I still had the chance.

396
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:22,580
If it wasn't for you two, we
wouldn't be where we are today.

397
00:22:24,100 --> 00:22:26,520
Well, I wouldn't go quite that far.

398
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:29,620
A lot of stuff happened,
but long story short,

399
00:22:29,840 --> 00:22:32,597
we ended up being trained by
Vice Admiral Garp himself.

400
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:34,445
That must have been hard work.

401
00:22:34,760 --> 00:22:38,637
Man, but you grew so much from
before, I didn't even recognize you.

402
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:39,550
It's crazy.

403
00:22:39,633 --> 00:22:42,920
The Koby I remember was
a pudgy little dorky guy.

404
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:48,337
I'm sure you're worn out
after all that happened.

405
00:22:48,420 --> 00:22:49,250
Sorry to bother you.

406
00:22:49,333 --> 00:22:50,280
Nah, it's fine.

407
00:22:50,460 --> 00:22:52,017
I haven't seen you in ages.

408
00:22:52,100 --> 00:22:53,320
We gotta celebrate.

409
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:55,420
Hey, you bastards!

410
00:22:55,740 --> 00:22:56,740
Hold on a second!

411
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:59,780
You didn't recognize me at all, huh?

412
00:23:00,300 --> 00:23:01,740
Who the hell are you?

413
00:23:02,860 --> 00:23:05,320
It's me! See? Me!

414
00:23:05,780 --> 00:23:06,900
No, I don't see.

415
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:07,950
Just tell me.

416
00:23:08,033 --> 00:23:09,740
Get a clue, guys.

417
00:23:12,280 --> 00:23:16,060
It's Helmepo, Captain
Morgan's son, Helmepo.

418
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:18,380
Surely you remember now.

419
00:23:18,520 --> 00:23:19,940
I had you tied up.

420
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:22,806
You were almost executed
because of me, Zoro.

421
00:23:23,020 --> 00:23:25,667
You couldn't possibly
forget that, could you?

422
00:23:27,340 --> 00:23:28,280
Well, there.

423
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:30,382
Now we all know who I am, right?

424
00:23:32,700 --> 00:23:33,740
Really, guys?

425
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:35,922
Stop giving me such a hard time.

426
00:23:36,780 --> 00:23:37,760
Now, now.

427
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:39,195
No one likes a bully.

428
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:43,220
Roro Noah Zoro, you seem
to be handling this well.

429
00:23:43,560 --> 00:23:44,620
Don't you agree?

430
00:23:45,440 --> 00:23:46,420
No! Stop!

431
00:23:46,860 --> 00:23:48,160
I worked so hard!

432
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:49,697
I made empty threats.

433
00:23:49,780 --> 00:23:51,920
I was always talking about my daddy.

434
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:55,780
Oh, that guy.

435
00:23:56,320 --> 00:23:57,908
What do you mean, that guy?

436
00:23:58,280 --> 00:23:59,337
Yeah, right.

437
00:23:59,420 --> 00:24:00,540
You sucked.

438
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:01,960
No wonder I forgot.

439
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:06,277
I wanted to forgive
them, but I just can't.

440
00:24:06,360 --> 00:24:07,860
I'm so sorry, Kobe.

441
00:24:08,140 --> 00:24:11,316
You just have to accept the
past and move on, Helmepo.

442
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:14,220
Now, I've got a job for you boys. Sir!

443
00:24:14,700 --> 00:24:18,580
This wall, fix it. What? Are you kidding?

444
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:22,197
If you were going to have us fix it,
why'd you break it in the first place?

445
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:25,097
Because walking through a door
doesn't make much of an impression.

446
00:24:25,180 --> 00:24:27,717
The only impression you're
making here is a bad one.

447
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:30,877
OK, we'll fix the wall, but it's
your fault, so you've got to help us.

448
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:31,790
What?

449
00:24:32,360 --> 00:24:33,190
All right.

450
00:24:38,040 --> 00:24:42,320
So this grandpa of yours
is really famous. Beats me.

451
00:24:42,580 --> 00:24:44,880
I never really asked him about his job.

452
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:53,940
By the way, Luffy, I heard you met
your old man a while back. Huh? My dad?

453
00:24:54,280 --> 00:24:55,880
No, I don't think so.

454
00:24:56,160 --> 00:24:58,240
I didn't even think I had a dad.

455
00:25:01,740 --> 00:25:02,700
That's a shame.

456
00:25:02,940 --> 00:25:05,293
I thought he'd introduce himself to you.

457
00:25:06,360 --> 00:25:09,242
From what I hear, he saw
you off back at Loguetown.

458
00:25:11,040 --> 00:25:11,870
Loguetown.

459
00:25:16,880 --> 00:25:20,821
I remember what happened, but I
sure don't remember Luffy's father.

460
00:25:21,900 --> 00:25:23,665
Could you give me a hint here?

461
00:25:23,880 --> 00:25:25,020
What's Dad like?

462
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:27,200
I'd like to know myself.

463
00:25:27,660 --> 00:25:29,180
I can't imagine it.

464
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:33,640
The name of your father is Monkey D.

465
00:25:33,860 --> 00:25:35,680
Dragon, the revolutionary.

466
00:25:40,600 --> 00:25:41,600
Dragon, huh?

467
00:25:51,640 --> 00:25:52,920
That dragon?

468
00:25:53,120 --> 00:25:55,060
The revolutionary has a son?

469
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:57,849
Even though he's famous,
Luffy didn't know.

470
00:25:58,680 --> 00:26:01,360
Wait, dragon is Vice Admiral Garp's son?

471
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:04,501
What kind of crazy messed
up family have they got?

472
00:26:04,700 --> 00:26:08,288
Come to think of it, I never
heard Dragon's full name before.

473
00:26:10,100 --> 00:26:11,517
What's the deal, you guys?

474
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:13,257
Why is everyone freaking out so much?

475
00:26:13,340 --> 00:26:14,217
Are you kidding?

476
00:26:14,300 --> 00:26:17,317
You're trying to tell me you've
never heard of Dragon before?

477
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:18,920
He's a dangerous man!

478
00:26:19,140 --> 00:26:20,640
Like, really dangerous!

479
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:25,340
Um, Robin?

480
00:26:25,840 --> 00:26:28,840
I'm not exactly sure how
I should explain this one.

481
00:26:29,600 --> 00:26:32,417
Pirates like us are enemies with the Navy,

482
00:26:32,500 --> 00:26:35,088
but we don't usually
attack them on our own.

483
00:26:35,480 --> 00:26:37,957
But there is one group that is directly

484
00:26:38,040 --> 00:26:40,757
opposing the authority
of the world government.

485
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:42,380
The Revolutionary Army.

486
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:45,520
And the man at the head
of that group is Dragon.

487
00:26:46,420 --> 00:26:50,832
By now his ideology has spread to many
nations causing worldwide rebellion.

488
00:26:51,060 --> 00:26:55,001
The government's hold has already
collapsed in a number of regions.

489
00:26:55,260 --> 00:26:57,317
Naturally, the government is furious.

490
00:26:57,400 --> 00:26:59,937
They've labeled Dragon as
the world's worst criminal

491
00:27:00,020 --> 00:27:03,138
and will stop at absolutely
nothing to hunt him down.

492
00:27:03,580 --> 00:27:06,897
The problem is that no one
knows a single thing about him.

493
00:27:06,980 --> 00:27:08,560
He's very mysterious.

494
00:27:09,640 --> 00:27:10,677
And yet...

495
00:27:10,760 --> 00:27:11,860
And yet what?

496
00:27:17,500 --> 00:27:19,840
Uh, that was a mistake, huh?

497
00:27:20,120 --> 00:27:22,826
I probably shouldn't
have said all that stuff.

498
00:27:33,100 --> 00:27:34,760
I take it all back.

499
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:36,300
Forget it, okay?

500
00:27:42,820 --> 00:27:43,650
What?
